# The stock report captured from the customer's DILOS instance is a byte-for-byte record of what
# that system actually sends, carriage returns included. Line-ending normalisation would rewrite it
# on the way into the repository, and the tests that assert the parser copes with CRLF would then
# be asserting it against a file that no longer has any.
#
# Deliberately scoped to this one file rather than to the fixture folder: the older stock report
# fixtures are stored with LF and checked out with CRLF, so exempting them from normalisation would
# make the next "git add" of one of them rewrite the stored blob.
tests/Lkv.WeClapp.Core.Tests/Fixtures/BE_20260828071116067.txt -text

# The frozen byte anchor of the AS delivery: what the renderer produced for the parity batch
# before the delivery moved onto the product's column renderer. Its assertions are about BYTES -
# 34 pipe fields per line, zero carriage returns, a final 0x0A - so line-ending normalisation
# would hand a fresh clone a file with a CR on every line and turn the anchor into a test that
# fails for a reason unrelated to any delivery, or worse, into one nobody trusts any more.
tests/AdapterMeshWeClapp.Tests/Fixtures/as-parity-expected.txt -text
